        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "33abde90e97e7084f7af8573224cc988250d64e7",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 464312120,
          "type": null,
          "body": "In ideal OS free'ing memory before exit should accelerate killing of process(es), because OS does a lot of checks for handlers. In practice it usually is not faster or even slower, but I can imagine some cases where it will be faster.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4334216,
            "username": "ValZapod",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Valerii Zapod.",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8cbd6d8ace62b0f9ddde773e6b7b781f0179e7b0a397aad45f4386db6d4dffbc?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/ValZapod"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-12-10T17:45:41.081Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-12-10T17:45:41.081Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 80826945,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1160,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "047d791436d9e9ff56108f6a9cc2902a38702411",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 464357287,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> In ideal OS free'ing memory before exit should accelerate killing of process(es),\n\nIn the OSes on which Wireshark runs (various UN\\*X flavors + Windows), the entire process address space is freed when the process terminates, so the memory allocator arena(s) to which freeing-before-exiting has returned a bunch of memory disappear, as does any the memory that *didn't* get freed before exiting.\n\n> because OS does a lot of checks for handlers\n\nYes, `exit()` (or returning from `main()`) will run `atexit()` handlers.  The former, at least, has no \"remove this handler\" call in ANSI C, so it's not as if you can prevent that.\n\nOr are you thinking of some other form of \"checks for handlers\"?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
